00:18:26,566 --> 00:18:28,866
the sweet potato roaster on a different show.

517
00:18:30,536 --> 00:18:31,536
And?

518
00:18:31,536 --> 00:18:33,276
(What does the experienced think?)

519
00:18:33,276 --> 00:18:34,376
And?

520
00:18:34,376 --> 00:18:35,546
The fat doesn't drain away.

521
00:18:37,146 --> 00:18:39,316
- Does it hold the fat?
- Is there a pool at the bottom?

522
00:18:39,316 --> 00:18:40,746
It might work...

523
00:18:40,946 --> 00:18:44,156
if you pre-cook the meat and render out the fat.

524
00:18:44,156 --> 00:18:47,556
But if you cook the raw meat, the aluminium foil rips apart...

525
00:18:47,556 --> 00:18:48,556
and sticks to the meat.

526
00:18:49,186 --> 00:18:50,856
(Realising)

527
00:18:51,526 --> 00:18:56,366
(The sweet potato roaster isn't suited to barbecuing raw meat.)

528
00:18:56,626 --> 00:18:58,666
But the owner is cooking it in front of us.

529
00:19:00,336 --> 00:19:01,866
He does look skilled at it.

530
00:19:01,866 --> 00:19:03,976
(The owner looks skilled at it.)

531
00:19:04,136 --> 00:19:05,276
May we go watch you?

532
00:19:05,536 --> 00:19:07,346
Of course, come over.

533
00:19:09,676 --> 00:19:11,276
I'll go, as an experienced cook.

534
00:19:11,276 --> 00:19:14,246
(Kyoung Pyo, the experienced, goes to investigate.)

535
00:19:14,846 --> 00:19:17,086
(Thinking)

536
00:19:17,316 --> 00:19:18,886
Kyoung Pyo says...

537
00:19:18,886 --> 00:19:19,886
there's nowhere for the fat to drain,

538
00:19:19,886 --> 00:19:21,686
- Right.
- so how does that work?

539
00:19:21,686 --> 00:19:23,056
- I modified it so that it could.
- Do you mind showing it to us?

540
00:19:23,356 --> 00:19:25,256
(Curious)

541
00:19:25,256 --> 00:19:27,366
- Do you mind showing it to us?
- I'll show it to you.

542
00:19:31,189 --> 00:19:33,359
- Do you mind showing it to us?
- I'll show it to you.

543
00:19:36,789 --> 00:19:37,799
It's whole pork belly.

544
00:19:37,799 --> 00:19:39,599
Does the meat really cook in here?

545
00:19:41,429 --> 00:19:42,729
What?

546
00:19:43,429 --> 00:19:45,539
- It looks good.
- My gosh.

547
00:19:45,539 --> 00:19:46,669
(Sweet potato roaster barbecue)

548
00:19:46,669 --> 00:19:47,839
- Does it?
- He placed wire racks...

549
00:19:47,839 --> 00:19:48,969
on the bottom.

550
00:19:48,969 --> 00:19:50,069
Yes, wire racks.

551
00:19:50,069 --> 00:19:51,109
He placed wire racks...

552
00:19:51,109 --> 00:19:52,439
- on the bottom.
- I see.

553
00:19:52,839 --> 00:19:54,779
He designed it so that...

554
00:19:54,779 --> 00:19:56,579
- the fat would drain to the bottom.
- To drain it.

555
00:19:56,579 --> 00:19:57,649
You're right.

556
00:19:58,219 --> 00:20:01,749
(The perfect Korean-style barbecue is ready to serve!)

557
00:20:02,249 --> 00:20:03,849
Here's what's suspicious.

558
00:20:03,849 --> 00:20:05,019
The meat doesn't look moist,

559
00:20:05,019 --> 00:20:07,989
as if the owner bought it somewhere else and put it inside.

560
00:20:07,989 --> 00:20:09,629
Aren't you crossing the line here?

561
00:20:09,929 --> 00:20:10,929
You've never met him before.

562
00:20:10,929 --> 00:20:12,629
- Isn't it normal on this show?
- What?

563
00:20:12,629 --> 00:20:13,699
Isn't it...

564
00:20:13,699 --> 00:20:14,799
You're supposed to question things,

565
00:20:14,799 --> 00:20:18,199
but not right in front of the owner. Got it?

566
00:20:18,199 --> 00:20:21,039
We can't help it if the owner hears us whispering about our suspicions,

567
00:20:21,039 --> 00:20:22,039
- Is that so?
- but don't say it...

568
00:20:22,039 --> 00:20:23,069
right to their face.

569
00:20:23,269 --> 00:20:25,439
(It's okay.)

570
00:20:25,579 --> 00:20:28,409
When I opened this compartment, it was empty.

571
00:20:28,409 --> 00:20:29,549
(Still passionately investigating)

572
00:20:29,849 --> 00:20:31,879
Business is slow because it's summer.

573
00:20:32,549 --> 00:20:34,119
(I simply made an inference.)

574
00:20:34,119 --> 00:20:35,489
Stop it. You're making us sad.

575
00:20:36,049 --> 00:20:38,159
I use both during the busy season.

576
00:20:38,159 --> 00:20:39,359
It's currently summer.

577
00:20:39,359 --> 00:20:41,659
- We'll taste it at our table.
- Okay.

578
00:20:41,659 --> 00:20:43,559
- You should taste it.
- Of course.

579
00:20:44,229 --> 00:20:46,859
(Setting up the table to try the barbecue)

580
00:20:48,029 --> 00:20:49,669
(Surprised)

581
00:20:49,669 --> 00:20:51,569
Is this the brand name?

582
00:20:52,599 --> 00:20:55,869
(Something is written on the spoon?)

583
00:20:56,039 --> 00:20:57,239
Why does it say Park Eun Bin?

584
00:20:58,939 --> 00:21:02,679
(Park Eun Bin is written on Jae Seok's spoon?)

585
00:21:02,809 --> 00:21:04,749
(Hyun Hee checks her spoon right away.)

586
00:21:04,749 --> 00:21:05,849
- What's this?
- What?

587
00:21:05,849 --> 00:21:07,319
- Mine says Lee Eun Ji.
- Eun Ji?

588
00:21:07,889 --> 00:21:09,089
Crush.

589
00:21:09,089 --> 00:21:10,119
- Crush?
- Crush?

590
00:21:10,619 --> 00:21:11,759
What's with these names?

591
00:21:11,759 --> 00:21:17,029
(Why are there names on the spoons?)

592
00:21:17,359 --> 00:21:18,359
Is this the hint?

593
00:21:18,529 --> 00:21:20,059
Could it be a hint?

594
00:21:20,059 --> 00:21:22,229
- Park Eun Bin. But it's a little...
- Son Heung Min.

595
00:21:22,229 --> 00:21:24,469
- They are all new.
- What do they have in common?

596
00:21:24,469 --> 00:21:25,899
I can see my reflection in it.

597
00:21:26,199 --> 00:21:29,169
(What do the names mean?)

598
00:21:29,509 --> 00:21:30,769
It's here.

599
00:21:31,039 --> 00:21:32,139
Already?

600
00:21:32,739 --> 00:21:34,679
Right. Here's your barbecue.

601
00:21:34,679 --> 00:21:35,809
- My gosh.
- Goodness.

602
00:21:36,609 --> 00:21:38,479
(A full plate)

603
00:21:38,979 --> 00:21:41,949
(Barbecue fresh out of the sweet potato roaster)

604
00:21:43,419 --> 00:21:44,459
It looks so good with all the extra fat...

605
00:21:44,459 --> 00:21:46,859
- rendered out.
- A barbecue platter.

606
00:21:48,389 --> 00:21:50,159
It looks amazing.

607
00:21:51,299 --> 00:21:53,599
I first season the meat with...

608
00:21:53,599 --> 00:21:55,169
a blend of ten ingredients.

609
00:21:55,829 --> 00:21:58,139
On top of it, I place bay leaves...

610
00:21:58,439 --> 00:21:59,839
so that the meat...

611
00:21:59,839 --> 00:22:01,869
has that smoky flavour when cooked.

612
00:22:02,239 --> 00:22:04,039
For extra moisture,

613
00:22:04,039 --> 00:22:05,379
I place green onions on the bottom.

614
00:22:06,509 --> 00:22:08,849
The seasoned meat goes on top of them.

615
00:22:08,849 --> 00:22:10,649
(The meat is ready to be grilled!)

616
00:22:10,649 --> 00:22:13,519
(It goes into the sweet potato roaster as is!)

617
00:22:13,619 --> 00:22:17,049
While maintaining the temperature at around 250°C to 300°C,

618
00:22:17,049 --> 00:22:18,419
I cook the meat for about 30 minutes.

619
00:22:19,159 --> 00:22:20,389
(Pork belly and galbi barbecued...)

620
00:22:20,389 --> 00:22:22,159
Pork belly and galbi. They look bomb.

621
00:22:22,159 --> 00:22:23,359
(in a sweet potato roaster)

622
00:22:23,559 --> 00:22:27,229
(Plate up the meat with an assortment of roasted vegetables.)

623
00:22:29,529 --> 00:22:30,699
It smells...

624
00:22:30,699 --> 00:22:33,499
(Sweet potato roaster barbecue, juicy and full of bite)

625
00:22:33,499 --> 00:22:34,869
Bon appetit.

626
00:22:36,939 --> 00:22:40,179
(Jae Seok tries a piece of meat first.)

627
00:22:40,179 --> 00:22:41,949
(Nodding enthusiastically)

628
00:22:42,779 --> 00:22:43,879
(Amazed)

629
00:22:43,879 --> 00:22:45,179
- Is it good?
- It's good.

630
00:22:45,749 --> 00:22:48,219
- With all that fat rendered out...
- It tastes clean.

631
00:22:48,819 --> 00:22:52,259
(Yu Ri tries the galbi.)

632
00:22:52,359 --> 00:22:54,759
(Impressed)

633
00:22:54,829 --> 00:22:57,529
It's not too tough, nor is it too greasy.

634
00:22:57,659 --> 00:23:00,799
It's chewy and moist. I'm loving it.

635
00:23:01,399 --> 00:23:03,469
The meat is perfect even without sauce.

636
00:23:03,469 --> 00:23:04,569
It's great.

637
00:23:05,599 --> 00:23:09,539
There's nothing suspicious about the taste.

638
00:23:09,639 --> 00:23:10,639
It's right up my alley.

639
00:23:10,639 --> 00:23:13,679
I often grill whole meat with an oven when I go camping.

640
00:23:13,679 --> 00:23:14,709
I see.

641
00:23:14,809 --> 00:23:16,279
It's much juicier than when I cook it,

642
00:23:16,279 --> 00:23:18,079
and it tastes like it was grilled by an expert.

643
00:23:18,079 --> 00:23:19,579
That's obvious.

644
00:23:19,749 --> 00:23:21,189
Isn't that obvious?

645
00:23:21,619 --> 00:23:22,649
What? What did she say?

646
00:23:22,649 --> 00:23:24,119
She said it was much juicier and more delicious...

647
00:23:24,119 --> 00:23:25,559
than when she cooked it.

648
00:23:25,559 --> 00:23:27,089
But shouldn't that be the case?

649
00:23:27,089 --> 00:23:28,689
(That should obviously be the case.)

650
00:23:29,189 --> 00:23:30,659
Or she should've opened a restaurant.

651
00:23:30,659 --> 00:23:31,929
(Or you should've opened a restaurant.)

652
00:23:31,929 --> 00:23:33,259
This is good.

653
00:23:33,359 --> 00:23:35,229
It's good. What's more, the meat is juicy.

654
00:23:35,499 --> 00:23:37,769
The meat is perfect even without sauce.

655
00:23:38,269 --> 00:23:40,239
I don't drink,

656
00:23:40,469 --> 00:23:42,209
but for those who like beer...

657
00:23:42,609 --> 00:23:44,539
It'll make the beer go down smoothly.

658
00:23:44,539 --> 00:23:47,309
The moment Hyoyeon had a bite, she said it'd be perfect with beer.

659
00:23:47,309 --> 00:23:48,579
It'd go well with beer.

660
00:23:48,679 --> 00:23:50,149
(Busy gnawing on a galbi)

661
00:23:50,149 --> 00:23:51,949
(Their eyes meet.)

662
00:23:51,949 --> 00:23:53,619
(Their eyes meet as Jae Seok pours some Coke.)

663
00:23:53,619 --> 00:23:54,649
(Laughing)

664
00:23:54,889 --> 00:23:56,119
Just as I was gnawing on it.

665
00:23:56,889 --> 00:23:58,459
I love the meat on the ribs.

666
00:23:58,459 --> 00:23:59,919
You looked really greedy like Nolbu just now.

667
00:24:00,719 --> 00:24:01,929
Just like Nolbu.

668
00:24:02,189 --> 00:24:03,989
She said you were just like Nolbu.

669
00:24:04,899 --> 00:24:06,399
(The Nolbu is intermittently feasting.)

670
00:24:06,399 --> 00:24:08,129
Even the enoki mushrooms are chewy.

671
00:24:08,429 --> 00:24:11,139
If we were to suspect something, what should we be suspicious of?

672
00:24:11,239 --> 00:24:13,239
The sweet potato roaster on the left...

673
00:24:13,239 --> 00:24:15,609
looked too new, with no grease on it.

674
00:24:15,609 --> 00:24:19,439
(The left sweet potato roaster had no grease whatsoever.)

675
00:24:21,549 --> 00:24:23,109
- It's seasoned well.
- So...

676
00:24:23,109 --> 00:24:24,179
Even if...

677
00:24:24,349 --> 00:24:26,549
- Yes, it looks too new.
- Right?

678
00:24:26,549 --> 00:24:28,989
The sweet potato roaster could've been put there at the last minute.

679
00:24:29,919 --> 00:24:31,119
(Surprised)

680
00:24:31,559 --> 00:24:33,019
What? No way.

681
00:24:33,019 --> 00:24:34,119
(The owner is serving another dish.)

682
00:24:34,529 --> 00:24:36,189
Why are you walking in looking so sad?

683
00:24:36,189 --> 00:24:37,959
(Laughing)

684
00:24:38,429 --> 00:24:40,329
(Unsteady)

685
00:24:40,799 --> 00:24:42,929
- Excuse me.
- Please don't give up. What...

686
00:24:42,929 --> 00:24:43,929
Oh, dear.

687
00:24:44,599 --> 00:24:46,039
You're making us feel bad.

688
00:24:47,399 --> 00:24:49,369
Will you stop walking in looking depressed, please?

689
00:24:49,369 --> 00:24:51,239
Business is slow during summer.

690
00:24:51,909 --> 00:24:53,979
(Repeating his joke)

691
00:24:54,139 --> 00:24:55,549
It'd be bad if I spilled it.

692
00:24:56,709 --> 00:24:58,479
When the meat gets a little too rich,

693
00:24:58,979 --> 00:25:00,549
try the jjamppong pasta.

694
00:25:00,549 --> 00:25:02,019
(The second dish is jjamppong pasta.)

695
00:25:02,019 --> 00:25:04,859
The customers kept asking for spicy soup.

696
00:25:05,759 --> 00:25:06,959
It's something I whipped up.

697
00:25:06,959 --> 00:25:09,759
(Another popular dish is the spicy jjamppong pasta.)

698
00:25:10,259 --> 00:25:11,299
The kick.

699
00:25:11,299 --> 00:25:12,899
I can feel the spiciness.

700
00:25:13,159 --> 00:25:16,099
(Trying a sip of the soup)

701
00:25:16,269 --> 00:25:17,529
(Amazed)

702
00:25:17,529 --> 00:25:18,639
It's delicious.

703
00:25:18,639 --> 00:25:20,999
(The noodle lover tries the noodles first.)

704
00:25:21,169 --> 00:25:23,939
(Savouring it)

705
00:25:24,339 --> 00:25:26,539
- My gosh, it has a kick.
- It's...

706
00:25:26,539 --> 00:25:28,349
It's jjamppong but with pasta noodles.

707
00:25:28,349 --> 00:25:30,909
- Really.
- The soup tastes like jjamppong.

708
00:25:30,909 --> 00:25:32,119
(Jjamppong made with pasta noodles)

709
00:25:32,619 --> 00:25:34,749
- What do you think?
- I haven't tried it yet.

710
00:25:34,749 --> 00:25:35,989
I'm still having the meat.

711
00:25:35,989 --> 00:25:38,259
For a second, I thought your dentures fell out.

712
00:25:39,859 --> 00:25:42,659
Something was coming out of the side of her mouth.

713
00:25:42,729 --> 00:25:44,859
(Laughing)

714
00:25:44,959 --> 00:25:46,629
- I am eating meat right now.
- Was it meat?

715
00:25:47,359 --> 00:25:48,869
I thought Yu Ri's dentures fell out.

716
00:25:48,869 --> 00:25:50,299
- She scared me.
- It was a bone.

717
00:25:50,299 --> 00:25:51,639
Was it a bone? I see.

718
00:25:51,739 --> 00:25:54,709
(Yu Ri feels wronged but still finds it funny.)

719
00:25:54,709 --> 00:25:57,339
(Jae Seok is completely satisfied.)

720
00:25:57,569 --> 00:25:59,209
I think this place is real.

721
00:25:59,279 --> 00:26:00,339
- Really?
- Everything is real.

722
00:26:00,339 --> 00:26:03,149
The owner seems like a great person.

723
00:26:03,149 --> 00:26:04,209
Right.

724
00:26:04,349 --> 00:26:05,479
He's a warm-hearted person,

725
00:26:05,479 --> 00:26:06,979
judging by how he feeds the stray cats.

726
00:26:06,979 --> 00:26:08,649
- I see.
- Everything here is real.

727
00:26:10,089 --> 00:26:11,919
- There's a cat outside.
- A kitten.

728
00:26:11,919 --> 00:26:13,159
- Three cats.
- My gosh.

729
00:26:13,159 --> 00:26:15,159
That's a real kitten.

730
00:26:15,259 --> 00:26:17,029
- A real baby cat.
- Gosh.

731
00:26:17,129 --> 00:26:19,799
- Really?
- Yes, it's just a little baby.

732
00:26:20,129 --> 00:26:21,429
It's so small.

733
00:26:21,629 --> 00:26:23,769
Sir, do you feed the cats?

734
00:26:23,869 --> 00:26:26,899
I've been feeding them food and treats.

735
00:26:27,839 --> 00:26:29,709
He actually feeds them.

736
00:26:29,709 --> 00:26:30,839
This place is real.

737
00:26:30,839 --> 00:26:34,449
(I'm telling you this place is real.)

738
00:26:35,009 --> 00:26:36,049
- It's real, - The owner...

739
00:26:36,049 --> 00:26:38,449
but business is just slow.

740
00:26:39,319 --> 00:26:40,819
- Yu Ri.
- I shouldn't say it, right?

741
00:26:40,819 --> 00:26:42,119
Business is slow only in summer.

742
00:26:42,119 --> 00:26:43,689
- Only in summer.
- Only in summer.

743
00:26:44,049 --> 00:26:45,759
He gets customers starting in fall.

744
00:26:47,019 --> 00:26:48,889
But you don't know that for sure.

745
00:26:48,889 --> 00:26:50,229
I'm quoting what the owner said.

746
00:26:50,289 --> 00:26:51,799
He said it while passing by.

747
00:26:51,799 --> 00:26:52,999
"Business is good in fall."

748
00:26:52,999 --> 00:26:54,599
(Laughing)

749
00:26:55,329 --> 00:26:58,439
(Business is good in fall.)

750
00:26:58,999 --> 00:27:01,169
(Is this place, where business booms in fall...)

751
00:27:01,169 --> 00:27:04,509
(according to the words of the owner, real?)

752
00:27:04,979 --> 00:27:06,779
I feel like the owner is real.

753
00:27:08,009 --> 00:27:11,149
The vibe the owner gives off and the food fit perfectly.

754
00:27:11,149 --> 00:27:12,249
(The food really matches the owner's vibe.)

755
00:27:12,619 --> 00:27:13,719
What do you think, Hyoyeon?

756
00:27:13,949 --> 00:27:15,589
The food is just so good.

757
00:27:15,989 --> 00:27:18,219
Having a full stomach is making me happy.

758
00:27:18,659 --> 00:27:19,789
Everything looks nice.

759
00:27:19,789 --> 00:27:21,759
(Everything looks nice.)

760
00:27:23,959 --> 00:27:25,629
Everything looks real, right?

761
00:27:26,099 --> 00:27:28,229
There's nothing to be suspicious about.

762
00:27:28,599 --> 00:27:30,229
- Let's get going.
- Okay.

763
00:27:30,229 --> 00:27:31,799
- Are we leaving already?
- Yes.

764
00:27:33,139 --> 00:27:34,969
- We have to eat at the next place.
- I see.

765
00:27:34,969 --> 00:27:36,069
Let's get going.

766
00:27:37,439 --> 00:27:39,179
What were those spoons?

767
00:27:39,209 --> 00:27:40,239
I forgot about them.

768
00:27:40,439 --> 00:27:42,379
Why were they made like that?

769
00:27:42,379 --> 00:27:44,409
Lee Eun Ji, Kim Ji Won, Park Eun Bin...

770
00:27:44,409 --> 00:27:45,579
Spoons with famous names.

771
00:27:45,579 --> 00:27:46,579
What kind of B-Side is it?

772
00:27:46,579 --> 00:27:47,819
The production crew...

773
00:27:47,819 --> 00:27:49,089
- could've set those up.
- Totally.

774
00:27:49,219 --> 00:27:50,389
- There is no...
- The names are of celebrities,

775
