1279
00:45:38,489 --> 00:45:40,189
I worked for three years.

1280
00:45:40,189 --> 00:45:43,089
Since it was a foreign company,

1281
00:45:43,089 --> 00:45:45,529
there were many events and parties.

1282
00:45:45,529 --> 00:45:48,759
I kept winning the talent shows.

1283
00:45:48,759 --> 00:45:50,199
I wanted to perform on a bigger stage...

1284
00:45:50,199 --> 00:45:51,629
and decided to take the comedian test.

1285
00:45:51,629 --> 00:45:52,939
I took it at 26.

1286
00:45:52,939 --> 00:45:54,469
(She passed the comedian test at the age of 26.)

1287
00:45:54,469 --> 00:45:55,569
That's late.

1288
00:45:55,569 --> 00:45:57,409
My colleagues all congratulated me.

1289
00:45:57,409 --> 00:46:00,409
They said I was the first worker to pursue my dream.

1290
00:46:00,509 --> 00:46:02,849
But I went back to the company after one year.

1291
00:46:02,849 --> 00:46:03,909
You went back?

1292
00:46:03,909 --> 00:46:05,749
- Really?
- The look they gave me was,

1293
00:46:05,749 --> 00:46:07,519
"As I thought."

1294
00:46:07,519 --> 00:46:08,519
You know what I mean?

1295
00:46:08,519 --> 00:46:10,449
They actually took you back in?

1296
00:46:10,449 --> 00:46:11,919
I went back as a contract worker.

1297
00:46:12,149 --> 00:46:14,819
I used to be a permanent worker, and I got a lot of benefit from it.

1298
00:46:14,819 --> 00:46:16,789
(From a permanent worker to a contract worker)

1299
00:46:16,789 --> 00:46:17,859
You went back as a contract worker.

1300
00:46:17,859 --> 00:46:20,559
I channelled that anger into my skit "The Red."

1301
00:46:20,859 --> 00:46:22,199
"Don't show off!"

1302
00:46:22,199 --> 00:46:23,199
(Laughing)

1303
00:46:23,199 --> 00:46:24,299
That anger.

1304
00:46:24,299 --> 00:46:26,499
(You're so funny.)

1305
00:46:27,399 --> 00:46:29,939
(I'm a university professor.)

1306
00:46:30,369 --> 00:46:33,339
(Don't show off.)

1307
00:46:33,809 --> 00:46:38,549
(She channelled her anger into comedy.)

1308
00:46:38,709 --> 00:46:40,749
That's how that skit came about.

1309
00:46:41,319 --> 00:46:43,489
So I'm grateful in a way.

1310
00:46:44,189 --> 00:46:45,589
We're in Jongno.

1311
00:46:46,159 --> 00:46:48,719
It was my turf back in school.

1312
00:46:50,589 --> 00:46:51,729
- What is it?
- What is it?

1313
00:46:52,499 --> 00:46:53,799
- Is this the place?
- "Chungkingmama?"

1314
00:46:54,229 --> 00:46:56,029
- "Chungkingmama?"
- "Mama?"

1315
00:46:56,029 --> 00:46:57,829
- "Chungkingmama?"
- Mama

1316
00:46:57,829 --> 00:46:58,899
Mama

1317
00:46:58,899 --> 00:47:00,439
(Mama, where is this?)

1318
00:47:00,439 --> 00:47:02,669
- Isn't it Chinese?
- Chinese?

1319
00:47:02,669 --> 00:47:03,939
Mala and so on.

1320
00:47:03,939 --> 00:47:06,609
(The third place gives off strong Chinese cuisine vibe.)

1321
00:47:06,979 --> 00:47:08,839
(It completely disappeared so fast.)

1322
00:47:08,839 --> 00:47:10,979
(I feel like we're at an amusement park.)

1323
00:47:12,179 --> 00:47:14,019
They sell cotton candy here?

1324
00:47:14,019 --> 00:47:15,019
(What's this place that disappears fast...)

1325
00:47:15,019 --> 00:47:16,049
(and is like an amusement park?)

1326
00:47:17,889 --> 00:47:18,889
What's this?

1327
00:47:20,359 --> 00:47:23,929
(Looking around)

1328
00:47:24,329 --> 00:47:27,559
This place has an incredible vibe.

1329
00:47:28,599 --> 00:47:30,169
It feels like Hong Kong.

1330
00:47:31,069 --> 00:47:33,299
(When you walk up the vibrant stairs...)

1331
00:47:34,299 --> 00:47:35,869
(Hong Kong-like interior design)

1332
00:47:35,869 --> 00:47:37,539
I want to go to Hong Kong.

1333
00:47:39,039 --> 00:47:41,779
It's so pretty here.

1334
00:47:41,779 --> 00:47:43,549
(Props that give off Hong Kong vibe)

1335
00:47:43,809 --> 00:47:46,219
(Looking around)

1336
00:47:48,379 --> 00:47:52,319
- There's a cotton candy machine.
- Where?

1337
00:47:52,719 --> 00:47:55,589
- There's a cotton candy machine.
- Where?

1338
00:47:55,659 --> 00:47:57,389
There's one over there.

1339
00:47:57,389 --> 00:48:01,929
(There really is a cotton candy machine as they deduced?)

1340
00:48:01,929 --> 00:48:04,899
There's a cotton candy machine.

1341
00:48:04,899 --> 00:48:08,399
- Exactly.
- That thing is steaming nonstop.

1342
00:48:09,239 --> 00:48:11,209
- What is that? Rice?
- Rice?

1343
00:48:11,209 --> 00:48:12,209
(The rice cooker in question keeps steaming.)

1344
00:48:12,209 --> 00:48:15,439
That makes the place look nicer.

1345
00:48:15,439 --> 00:48:17,309
Yes, that one thing makes it look nicer.

1346
00:48:18,109 --> 00:48:19,949
It really feels like I'm in Hong Kong.

1347
00:48:19,949 --> 00:48:21,349
(It feels more dreamy thanks to the steam.)

1348
00:48:21,779 --> 00:48:25,089
(Consistent concept and props, is this place real?)

1349
00:48:25,219 --> 00:48:26,419
This place is real.

1350
00:48:26,419 --> 00:48:28,459
You look very tired.

1351
00:48:29,229 --> 00:48:31,029
You're having a blood sugar spike, aren't you?

1352
00:48:31,029 --> 00:48:32,559
I shouldn't have drunk mugwort latte.

1353
00:48:32,829 --> 00:48:35,199
- Which one?
- Mugwort latte.

1354
00:48:35,329 --> 00:48:37,669
The sweetness hit me strongly.

1355
00:48:38,369 --> 00:48:40,139
- Shall we invite the owner?
- Sir.

1356
00:48:40,139 --> 00:48:41,469
It feels like I should speak Mandarin.

1357
00:48:41,899 --> 00:48:43,739
- Thank you.
- Hello.

1358
00:48:44,139 --> 00:48:45,609
- Hello.
- Hello.

1359
00:48:45,609 --> 00:48:46,709
Hello.

1360
00:48:46,779 --> 00:48:49,009
Hello, sir. Please stand here.

1361
00:48:49,149 --> 00:48:52,109
I really like the vibe here.

1362
00:48:52,109 --> 00:48:53,549
What do you sell here?

1363
00:48:53,549 --> 00:48:57,289
Hong Kong has a culture called cha chaan teng.

1364
00:48:57,549 --> 00:49:02,289
It's a Hong Kong-style restaurant with cha chaan teng.

1365
00:49:02,529 --> 00:49:06,999
No wonder the place looks like a scene from a Hong Kong movie.

1366
00:49:07,259 --> 00:49:10,229
In one sentence, it's small Hong Kong in Seoul.

1367
00:49:10,229 --> 00:49:13,739
I based it off the Tsim Sha Tsui night market.

1368
00:49:13,739 --> 00:49:15,099
(Tsim Sha Tsui: Hong Kong's famous tourist spot)

1369
00:49:15,099 --> 00:49:18,409
I got the props to suit the mood too.

1370
00:49:19,069 --> 00:49:22,009
The motif of the restaurant is "Chungking Express."

1371
00:49:22,849 --> 00:49:24,679
There's a scene where they express their love...

1372
00:49:24,679 --> 00:49:26,479
with a fish tank in between them.

1373
00:49:26,479 --> 00:49:28,879
I got the water tank based on that.

1374
00:49:29,189 --> 00:49:32,789
I also got a sofa similar to the one...

1375
00:49:32,789 --> 00:49:34,689
in the movie.

1376
00:49:36,429 --> 00:49:41,299
(Props from the scenes of "Chungking Express")

1377
00:49:41,299 --> 00:49:43,899
Did you live in Hong Kong?

1378
00:49:43,899 --> 00:49:46,139
I wanted to, but I couldn't.

1379
00:49:46,139 --> 00:49:47,469
I only went to Hong Kong on a site visit.

1380
00:49:47,539 --> 00:49:48,539
(I see.)

1381
00:49:49,669 --> 00:49:51,569
Everyone is pretty frank today.

1382
00:49:53,409 --> 00:49:56,009
All the owners are very honest.

1383
00:49:56,009 --> 00:49:58,809
Which dish is popular here?

1384
00:49:58,809 --> 00:50:01,319
I have two unique dishes.

1385
00:50:01,319 --> 00:50:03,989
I have levitating noodles and cloud guobaorou.

1386
00:50:03,989 --> 00:50:06,789
Cloud guobaorou and levitating noodles?

1387
00:50:06,789 --> 00:50:08,659
- Levitating?
- Levitating?

1388
00:50:08,859 --> 00:50:11,029
I enjoyed watching Monkey King...

1389
00:50:11,029 --> 00:50:13,229
and admired him riding Flying Nimbus, the cloud,

1390
00:50:13,229 --> 00:50:14,959
so I got an inspiration from it.

1391
00:50:14,959 --> 00:50:17,729
I used cotton candy for the sweetness,

1392
00:50:17,729 --> 00:50:20,039
and thus, the dish was born.

1393
00:50:20,539 --> 00:50:24,039
As for the levitating noodles, when I went to Hong Kong,

1394
00:50:24,039 --> 00:50:26,679
I came across a dish which had fried noodles standing up...

1395
00:50:26,679 --> 00:50:29,479
at a very famous cha chaan teng restaurant.

1396
00:50:29,849 --> 00:50:31,209
Isn't this Hong Kong?

1397
00:50:31,549 --> 00:50:34,919
It looks so much like Hong Kong that my eyes popped out.

1398
00:50:34,979 --> 00:50:37,819
Sixth Sense crew, is this place real?

1399
00:50:41,719 --> 00:50:44,429
- Could we try the dishes?
- I'll prepare them right away.

1400
00:50:44,429 --> 00:50:45,429
Thank you.

1401
00:50:45,429 --> 00:50:46,429
(How does cloud guobaorou look like?)

1402
00:50:46,429 --> 00:50:49,729
I have a feeling it's a perfect beer snack.

1403
00:50:49,729 --> 00:50:51,599
- You can smell mala too, right?
- Yes.

1404
00:50:51,599 --> 00:50:52,939
- Right?
- It's very strong.

1405
00:50:53,169 --> 00:50:55,369
But there's no Korean...

1406
00:50:55,369 --> 00:50:57,209
on the menu. Would it be okay?

1407
00:50:57,209 --> 00:50:58,909
I can only read that. "Liquor."

1408
00:50:59,109 --> 00:51:00,209
- Liquor...
- Liquor?

1409
00:51:00,209 --> 00:51:02,179
You can only read that. Beer.

1410
00:51:02,179 --> 00:51:03,179
(The menu is full of Chinese, no Korean.)

1411
00:51:03,179 --> 00:51:05,279
"Gagugarak" is Coca Cola, right?

1412
00:51:05,649 --> 00:51:07,449
- Coca Cola.
- Coca Cola.

1413
00:51:07,449 --> 00:51:08,479
(A transliteration of Coca Cola,)

1414
00:51:08,479 --> 00:51:09,519
(which means it tastes good and it's fun)

1415
00:51:09,949 --> 00:51:11,619
What does "gagugara" mean?

1416
00:51:12,189 --> 00:51:13,589
"Take it and go?"

1417
00:51:14,319 --> 00:51:17,429
It's fun when you put it in your mouth.

1418
00:51:18,129 --> 00:51:19,799
That's why that character, meaning "fun," is used.

1419
00:51:20,629 --> 00:51:23,399
He's starting.

1420
00:51:23,399 --> 00:51:26,839
(The owner starts to make cotton candy.)

1421
00:51:28,699 --> 00:51:29,809
(When he adds sugar, white thread is formed.)

1422
00:51:29,809 --> 00:51:31,709
He really is making cotton candy.

1423
00:51:33,579 --> 00:51:34,609
White sugar.

1424
00:51:35,539 --> 00:51:37,579
Cotton candy is hard to make...

1425
00:51:38,079 --> 00:51:40,219
if you don't have the experience.

1426
00:51:41,149 --> 00:51:42,619
The wrist snap is very important.

1427
00:51:42,619 --> 00:51:43,819
It's very important.

1428
00:51:43,819 --> 00:51:45,149
(The owner's hands move with practised ease.)

1429
00:51:45,149 --> 00:51:46,819
Just in case, should we ask for a rabbit?

1430
00:51:46,819 --> 00:51:47,859
- What?
- Let's do that.

1431
00:51:48,089 --> 00:51:49,729
Please make it in the shape of a rabbit.

1432
00:51:49,729 --> 00:51:50,859
Can you make Pikachu?

1433
00:51:52,589 --> 00:51:56,069
(Pretending not to hear it with all his might)

1434
00:51:56,499 --> 00:51:58,799
That wrist snap of his... Right?

1435
00:51:58,799 --> 00:52:00,739
I know. This can't be his first time doing it.

1436
00:52:00,739 --> 00:52:02,239
You can tell he's been doing this for three years.

1437
00:52:02,909 --> 00:52:04,469
It's shaped like a cloud.

1438
00:52:06,209 --> 00:52:07,979
- It looks insane.
- My goodness.

1439
00:52:07,979 --> 00:52:10,479
(Impressed)

1440
00:52:11,009 --> 00:52:12,649
(Fascinated)

1441
00:52:13,949 --> 00:52:15,279
Here's your food.

1442
00:52:16,089 --> 00:52:17,319
What is this?

1443
00:52:19,002 --> 00:52:20,742
- It looks insane.
- My goodness.

1444
00:52:20,742 --> 00:52:23,312
(Impressed)

1445
00:52:23,742 --> 00:52:25,472
(Fascinated)

1446
00:52:26,812 --> 00:52:28,082
Here's your food.

1447
00:52:28,742 --> 00:52:30,212
What is this?

1448
00:52:31,982 --> 00:52:36,222
(A blanket of cotton candy, gently placed over the guobaorou)

1449
00:52:36,222 --> 00:52:38,552
So you pour the sauce over this.

1450
00:52:38,552 --> 00:52:41,022
This will double the sweetness.

1451
00:52:41,192 --> 00:52:42,932
Kids would absolutely love this.

1452
00:52:42,932 --> 00:52:45,262
They will love it so much.

1453
00:52:45,262 --> 00:52:48,862
(Visuals that would charm anyone)

1454
00:52:48,862 --> 00:52:50,102
For the cloud guobaorou,

1455
00:52:50,102 --> 00:52:52,132
I use Korean pork loin,

1456
00:52:52,132 --> 00:52:55,002
coat it in a batter I developed, and deep-fry in oil.

1457
00:52:55,002 --> 00:52:56,212
(It's coated in a starch batter and deep-fried in oil.)

1458
00:52:57,372 --> 00:52:59,682
I serve it topped with homemade cotton candy...

1459
00:52:59,682 --> 00:53:02,952
and a green plum sauce on the side.

1460
00:53:04,652 --> 00:53:05,812
This is fascinating.

1461
00:53:05,982 --> 00:53:07,322
I'm so curious about the taste.

1462
00:53:07,322 --> 00:53:08,722
(Cloud guobaorou)

1463
00:53:08,882 --> 00:53:10,492
I'll pour the sauce over it for you.

1464
00:53:10,492 --> 00:53:11,492
- Okay.
- Then...

1465
00:53:11,492 --> 00:53:13,862
- It will vanish just like a cloud.
- Exactly.

1466
00:53:14,762 --> 00:53:16,632
I used finely ground green plums...

1467
00:53:16,732 --> 00:53:18,362
to maximize the texture.

1468
00:53:20,732 --> 00:53:23,872
So you made the tangsuyuk sauce with cotton candy.

1469
00:53:23,872 --> 00:53:25,772
That's a brilliant idea.

1470
00:53:26,202 --> 00:53:28,042
(Once the cotton candy melts, the guobaorou appears.)

1471
00:53:28,042 --> 00:53:29,142
My goodness.

1472
00:53:29,142 --> 00:53:31,142
- That's a brilliant idea.
- This has to be delicious.

1473
00:53:31,472 --> 00:53:32,742
It looks so cute.

1474
00:53:32,742 --> 00:53:33,912
- Kids would love this.
- Seriously,

1475
00:53:33,912 --> 00:53:35,982
- the owners amaze me all the time.
- I know.

1476
00:53:35,982 --> 00:53:37,612
- It's astonishing.
- It's...

1477
00:53:37,612 --> 00:53:39,352
- all about creativity.
- Right.

1478
00:53:39,352 --> 00:53:40,922
There's no way this isn't delicious.

1479
00:53:41,022 --> 00:53:43,152
Because it doubles the sweetness.

1480
00:53:43,322 --> 00:53:45,152
All right. Let's try it.

1481
00:53:45,152 --> 00:53:46,592
(Just look at the colour.)

1482
00:53:46,862 --> 00:53:48,092
- Hyoyeon.
- Yes?

1483
00:53:48,092 --> 00:53:49,092
Thank you.

1484
00:53:50,392 --> 00:53:51,392
(Chuckling)

1485
00:53:51,392 --> 00:53:52,632
- Seriously...
- Thank you.

1486
00:53:52,632 --> 00:53:54,662
I thought Hyoyeon was from another country.

1487
00:53:55,362 --> 00:53:58,232
There are still a lot of people who talk to me in English.

1488
00:53:58,232 --> 00:53:59,302
I feel so uncomfortable.

1489
00:53:59,702 --> 00:54:01,442
She's uncomfortable because people speak English.

1490
00:54:01,442 --> 00:54:03,512
(She's a native Korean from Incheon.)

1491
00:54:03,642 --> 00:54:05,372
- Let's try it first.
- Okay.

1492
00:54:05,372 --> 00:54:07,742
(How does the cloud guobaorou taste?)

1493
00:54:07,742 --> 00:54:09,982
- Taste it first.
- I'll try it.

1494
00:54:09,982 --> 00:54:14,022
(Taking a bite, soaked in sauce)

1495
00:54:15,152 --> 00:54:16,152
(Exclaiming)

1496
00:54:18,352 --> 00:54:21,322
(The brow never lies.)

1497
00:54:21,762 --> 00:54:23,532
It has a slight tang.

1498
00:54:23,832 --> 00:54:24,992
- And...
- It's good, isn't it?

1499
00:54:25,462 --> 00:54:28,762
With cotton candy on top, you'd think it's too sweet, but...

1500
00:54:28,932 --> 00:54:30,402
It's not that sweet.

1501
00:54:31,272 --> 00:54:34,142
The sugar replaces corn syrup to bring out the sweetness.

1502
00:54:34,142 --> 00:54:36,042
(The perfect harmony of cotton candy and guobaorou)

1503
00:54:36,142 --> 00:54:38,142
It's actually tangier.

1504
00:54:38,142 --> 00:54:39,442
Maybe because of the green plum?

1505
00:54:39,442 --> 00:54:42,342
The tangy kick from the green plum makes it even tastier.

1506
00:54:42,342 --> 00:54:44,412
(Tangy green plums cut through the sweetness of the cotton candy.)

1507
00:54:44,552 --> 00:54:48,852
(Savouring with his nose first)

1508
00:54:55,022 --> 00:54:58,662
(Kyoung Pyo, are you asleep?)

1509
00:54:58,932 --> 00:55:00,532
He's not sleeping with his eyes shut, is he?

1510
00:55:01,632 --> 00:55:05,632
(His unique way of tasting food)

1511
00:55:06,272 --> 00:55:07,742
I thought it'd be really sweet.

1512
00:55:07,742 --> 00:55:08,742
- But it's not.
- It's not that sweet.

1513
00:55:08,742 --> 00:55:10,272
It's not overly sweet at all.

1514
00:55:10,572 --> 00:55:12,912
When you have something too sweet, everything else tastes mild, right?

1515
00:55:13,842 --> 00:55:15,442
(Yum)

1516
00:55:16,212 --> 00:55:18,582
Hyun Hee, you're eating a lot today.

1517
00:55:18,582 --> 00:55:20,582
(Hyun Hee, you're eating a lot today.)

1518
00:55:21,152 --> 00:55:22,722
This tastes incredible.

1519
00:55:23,492 --> 00:55:25,322
I thought you lost your appetite.

1520
00:55:26,192 --> 00:55:27,962
With the dishes constantly changing,

1521
00:55:28,392 --> 00:55:30,092
my brain resets with novelty.

1522
00:55:31,032 --> 00:55:33,062
- Okay.
- That's why I keep eating.

1523
00:55:33,062 --> 00:55:34,862
- This is nice.
- I'm glad you're eating well.

1524
00:55:35,402 --> 00:55:36,502
Levitating!

1525
00:55:36,872 --> 00:55:38,202
- What?
- It's unbelievable.

1526
00:55:38,472 --> 00:55:40,602
(What is this?)

1527
00:55:40,942 --> 00:55:42,202
This makes no sense.

1528
00:55:43,242 --> 00:55:44,442
- What?
- It's unbelievable.

1529
00:55:45,012 --> 00:55:46,912
- This makes no sense.
- Gosh!

1530
00:55:47,342 --> 00:55:48,482
